  "question": {
    "text": "A small particle of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and its retaining cord is spinning with angular velocity <math><mi>ω</mi></math> on the horizontal surface of a smooth disc. As force&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> is slightly relaxed,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> increases and <math><mi>ω</mi></math> changes. Determine the rate of change of <math><mi>ω</mi></math> with respect to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math><br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0016_cbde99654be7.jpeg\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 215px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi> </mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "During the motion of the object, there is only one force tension which is acting towards a fixed point (centre of the table - disc). So that motion is under the effect to central force and thus, angular momentum will be conserved. At any radial distance,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>m&#969;r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>dL</mi><mi>dr</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>mr</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfrac><mi>d&#969;</mi><mi>dr</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>m&#969;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><br />So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>d&#969;</mi><mi>dr</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mfrac></math>"
  }
}